Multi-request session for the proxy prover. Applies to tlsnotary/tlsn
47aee45b53e06648c1b2ad3689b367b8c923fdec (v0.1.0-alpha.15) after
0001-await-io-write.patch.

Adds, and changes nothing that exists: `SdkProver::send_requests_proxy` in
sdk-core and `Prover.send_requests(server_io, requests)` in the wasm bindings.
The requests are sent in order over ONE TLS connection through hyper's single
HTTP/1.1 connection, without pipelining: each response is read to its end
before the next request is written, so the transcript is req1 resp1 req2
resp2 of one session. The caller's last request carries `connection: close`
(the schema package builds it). Every response is returned. The prover is left
`Committed`, exactly as after `send_request`, for the same `transcript()` and
`reveal()`. Every request is built before the connection opens. Multi-request headers are
inserted in normalized name order after the existing validation, avoiding the
independent HashMap order of each request. Header names and values are preserved. Proxy mode
only; `server_io` must be omitted. `send_request`, the protocol, the
commitments, the reveal and the verifier are untouched.

